{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Board diligence checklist**\n\n- **Licence:** Identify parties and sublicensing rights; term, automatic renewal, nonrenewal deadlines, termination triggers, cure periods, fees, indemnities, liability limits, assignment/change-of-control provisions, and post-termination data and transition rights.\n- **Naming dependencies:** Map rights to the index name, provider name and trademarks across fund names, disclosures and marketing. Determine when rights expire and what renaming, rebranding and investor communications would follow.\n- **Failed renewal:** Verify whether replacement requires consent or a new licence; assess tracking continuity, trading costs, tax effects and operational readiness. Check investment-objective/fundamental-policy constraints, board or shareholder approvals, disclosure updates and exchange-listing requirements. Do not assume substitution is permitted.\n- **Affiliated information:** Map ownership and business relationships among provider, adviser and affiliates. Examine methodology/rebalancing conflicts, advance access to index changes or portfolio information, information barriers, trading controls, selective disclosure and oversight.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Notice periods and substitution rights depend on the actual contracts and fund documents."}}
